From: Package maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] bus: load transient configuration before administrator policy
Source: https://dbus.freedesktop.org/releases/dbus/dbus-1.16.2.tar.xz
Upstream: Not submitted; this adds the conventional Linux /run policy tier.

D-Bus already keeps its package defaults in /usr/share/dbus-1 and loads
administrator policy from /etc/dbus-1. Add the corresponding /run/dbus-1
drop-in directories between those two tiers. This gives image builders and
early-boot tools a transient policy location without writing persistent host
configuration.

Merge the drop-in family instead of scanning three directories independently.
include_dir() walked each directory with readdir and included every .conf it
found, so a higher tier could not replace a same-named lower file and a link to
/dev/null did not mask one. Add an <includedirs> element whose handler walks the
vendor, /run, and /etc trees for one family, lets a higher tree replace a
basename, treats a non-regular file such as a /dev/null link as a mask, sorts
the survivors, and includes them in that order. The bus configuration files now
name the family once instead of listing three directories.
